{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed from Beth-el, and there was still a stretch of land to come to Ephrath.</b> Ephrath is Bethlehem, as it says (Genesis 35:19): ״ותקבר בדרך אפרתה היא בית לחם״. And Ramban, z.l., testified that he saw with his own eyes that from the tomb of Rachel to Bethlehem there is not even a mil. If so, the explanation they gave for the word כברת ארץ — that it is of the language of כביר, meaning 'much,' because there is a great distance between them — is not correct. Rather, it is a term of measurement, according to the words of Rashi, z.l.: for כברת is like ברת, and the כ is a prefix of use, not radical; and it is a name for a known measure in those days."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:48.289590414Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}